  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Which one of the following reactions does not occur during extraction of copper ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "moJ10",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "85wO7",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>FeS</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>FeO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TjkCR",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CaO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CaSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lGYdh",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The following changes occur during smelting.</p><p>(a) Most of the&nbsp;ferrous sulphide gets oxidised to ferrous oxide which combines with silica (flux) to form fusible slag.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>FeS</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>FeO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;(Ferrous silicate)</p><p>The slag being lighter floats and forms the upper layer. It is removed through the slag hole from time to time.</p><p>(b)&nbsp;During roasting or in the blast furnace if any oxide of copper is formed, it combines with FeS and is changed back into its sulphide.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>FeS</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>FeO</mi></math></p><p>Ferrous oxide thus formed again combines with silica to form more slag.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>So, no formation of calcium silicate&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>CaSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;extraction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi></math>.</p>",
